From cab0a2065cbf63a1106883ec4d32926759365953 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emanuel Ehmki <emanuel.ehmki@pfizer.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Apr 2026 17:20:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] session: restore Ripgrep.defaultLayer in prompt defaultLayer

The skill-preamble auto-load helpers consume Ripgrep.Service via
`const rg = yield* Ripgrep.Service` in session/prompt.ts, but the integrate
merge for local/skill-preamble drops `Ripgrep.defaultLayer` from the
Layer.mergeAll(...) block at the bottom of prompt.ts when reconciling
imports with the earlier local/intelligent-session-watchdog merge. The
import line for Ripgrep survives (the merge keeps it alongside Git/Skill/
Glob) but the layer provision is lost, leaving the consumer unsatisfied
and producing a runtime error on every opencode invocation:

    Service not found: @opencode/Ripgrep

Pre-catch-up local-integrated carried a `session: restore Ripgrep.defaultLayer
in prompt` commit (053c94236a) that added this same line; that commit was
not promoted to any standalone branch because the deletion happens only
during integration, not on any source branch.

This patch is applied automatically by rebuild-local-dev.sh AFTER the
local/skill-preamble merge, restoring Ripgrep.defaultLayer to the
Layer.mergeAll(...) provide chain alongside Skill.defaultLayer, Git.defaultLayer,
and CrossSpawnSpawner.defaultLayer.
---
 packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts b/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts
--- a/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts
+++ b/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts
@@ -1915,6 +1915,7 @@ export const defaultLayer = Layer.suspend(() =>
         LLM.defaultLayer,
         Git.defaultLayer,
         Skill.defaultLayer,
+        Ripgrep.defaultLayer,
         Bus.layer,
         CrossSpawnSpawner.defaultLayer,
       ),
--
